  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0149' contains 7 tables.\nThe 'user' table represents a user of the system, with columns for 'user_id', 'username', 'password', 'email', 'avatar', 'nickname', 'registration_time', 'role_id', and 'category_id'. These columns do not allow null values and are the primary key for this table. The 'role_id' and 'category_id' columns are foreign keys referencing the 'role' and 'category' tables respectively, with on delete and on update cascade rules.\nThe 'role' table represents a role in the system, with columns for 'role_id', 'role_name', 'role_description', and 'permission'. These columns do not allow null values and are the primary key for this table. The 'permission' column is a foreign key referencing the 'permission' table, with on delete and on update cascade rules.\nThe 'permission' table represents a permission in the system, with columns for 'permission_id', 'permission_name', 'permission_description', and 'role_id'. These columns do not allow null values and are the primary key for this table.\nThe 'notification' table represents a notification in the system, with columns for 'notification_id', 'notification_title', 'notification_content', 'sending_time', and 'receiving_user_id'. These columns do not allow null values and are the primary key for this table. The 'receiving_user_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'user' table, with on delete and on update cascade rules.\nThe 'request' table represents a request in the system, with columns for 'request_id', 'request_content', 'request_time', 'request_status', and 'user_id'. These columns do not allow null values and are the primary key for this table. The 'user_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'user' table, with on delete and on update cascade rules.\nThe 'category' table represents a category in the system, with columns for 'category_id', 'category_name', and 'category_description'. These columns do not allow null values and are the primary key for this table.\nFinally, the 'to-do_item' table represents a to-do item in the system, with columns for 'item_id', 'item_content', 'item_status', 'creation_time', 'deadline', and 'user_id'. These columns do not allow null values and are the primary key for this table. The 'user_id' column is a foreign key referencing the 'user' table, with on delete and on update cascade rules.\nThis schema ensures entity integrity by having primary keys and foreign keys, and referential integrity by having cascade delete and update rules.",
  "gold_question": "The User Management System is designed to manage user-related information and functionalities. The primary functions include:\n1.User Management: This includes adding, modifying, deleting, and querying user information. Each user has a User ID, Username, Password, Email, Avatar, Nickname, and Registration Time. Each user is assigned a specific Role and Category.\n2.Role Management: Defines different roles and their associated permissions.\n3.Permission Management: Assigns different operation permissions to different roles. Each role includes Role ID, Role Name, and Role Description.\n4.Notification Management: Sends and manages notifications to users, including Notification Title, Notification Content, and Sending Time.\n5.Request Management: Handles user requests. Each request includes Request Content, Request Time, and Request Status.\n6.Category Management: Organizes user data into categories, including Category Name and Category Description.\n7.To-Do Management: Manages the creation, modification, deletion, and querying of user to-do items. Each to-do item includes Item ID, Item Content, Item Status, Creation Time, and Deadline.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0149.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0149\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `nickname` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`role_id`) REFERENCES `role` (`role_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`category_id`) REFERENCES `category` (`category_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `role` (\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `role_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role_description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `permission` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`role_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `role_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`permission`) REFERENCES `permission` (`permission_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `permission` (\n  `permission_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `permission_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `permission_description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`permission_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `notification` (\n  `notification_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `notification_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `notification_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `sending_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `receiving_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`notification_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `notification_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`receiving_user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `request` (\n  `request_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `request_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `request_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `request_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`request_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `request_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `category` (\n  `category_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `category_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category_description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`category_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `to-do_item` (\n  `item_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `item_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `item_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `deadline` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`item_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `to-do_item_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
